<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2312/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2312/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2312/>;
    dc:modified '2026-06-18T12:16:31'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Sercon Integra2 EA-IRMS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sercon Integra2 Elemental Analysis-Isotope Ratio Mass Spectrometer system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A combination of the Sercon HS2022 mass spectrometer and the EArth elemental analyser, designed to perform a dual isotopic enrichment analysis (13C/15N) and to measure both POC, PON, Carbon uptake and N2 fixation. During operation, a capsule containing the sample falls into the combustion tube and is converted in the presence of oxygen to CO2, N2, NO2, and H2. An elemental copper stage reduces NOx, a MgCIO4 trap removes water vapour, a switchable EMAsorb trap can be used to remove CO2 (for 15N only analysis) and a GC column separates CO2 from N2 (allowing dual isotope analysis). Organic 18O analysis is possible by analysing CO. An 34S option is also available. It has a software controlled pneumatic autosampler - Optional carousels include 180 samples (5mm diameter), 120 samples (8mm diameter), or 80 samples (12 mm diameter).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2312'^^xsd:string .
